cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295\n  modified: 2026-07-27T07:36:05.431Z\n---\n\nFound and fixed 2026-07-27, shipped in cledger 0.13.0 (on main, `47e117b`).\n\n`findRepo` used `git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir`, which in a linked worktree\nreturns that worktree's *private* dir (`<main>/.git/worktrees/<name>/`). Git\nbehaves as documented; the wrong assumption was that a repo has one git dir.\nNothing cledger stores there is per-worktree, so a worktree acted like a\nseparate repo. Severity order as found:\n\n1. Pre-push hook installed where **git never runs it** — git resolves hooks\n   against the common dir only. A repo whose first capture happened in a\n   worktree got a hook that looked installed and silently never fired.\n2. known-secrets store invisible → failed **open**: learned secrets written to\n   the ledger in the clear, nothing reporting it.\n3. allowlist invisible → failed closed: 213 findings from a worktree vs 0 from\n   the main checkout of this repo.\n4. cursors reset → transcripts re-scanned from the top.\n\n**Fix:** `RepoInfo.commonDir` from `--path-format=absolute --git-common-dir`\n(manual-resolve fallback for git < 2.31); all state + hook path hang off it.\n`gitDir` kept but documented as a trap. Worktree *placement* is irrelevant —\ngit treats nested and arbitrary-path worktrees identically.\n\n**Consequence that outlived the cause:** symptom 4 also *duplicated events*.\nAppend-time dedup only reads the note of the commit being written to, so a\nrescan after HEAD moved filed a second copy under a different anchor — 351\nduplicated ids in this repo's ledger, and reads returned them twice. Ledger is\nappend-only, so those are permanent; fixed on the read side (`dedupById`,\nearliest `recorded_at` wins, canonical JSON tie-break). **Not\nworktree-specific** — any forced rescan after HEAD moves reproduces it.\n\n**Deliberately unchanged:** `.cledger.json` is a tracked working-tree file, so\nit is per-worktree unless committed. Correct for versioned repo config.\n\n**Not migrated:** allowlist/known-secrets written from a worktree pre-0.13.0\nstay orphaned in that worktree's private dir.\n\nSee [[project-cledger-agent-provenance]], [[project-cledger-redaction-state]].\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-worktree-gitdir.md","memdirStamped":true,"originalFile":"---\nname: project-cledger-worktree-gitdir\ndescription: \"cledger's per-repo local state is invisible from a git worktree — allowlist/cursors/known-secrets keyed on --absolute-git-dir\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295\n  modified: 2026-07-27T07:19:17.141Z\n---\n\nFound 2026-07-27, unfixed. `findRepo` in `src/git.ts` sets `gitDir` from\n`git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir`, which in a worktree returns\n`.git/worktrees/<name>/`, not the shared `.git/`. All per-repo local state\nhangs off that path — `conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`,\n`known-secrets.json`, `cursors/`, `reanchor-cursor`, the pending queue.\n\n**Symptoms, worst first:**\n1. `installHook` writes to `repo.gitDir/hooks/pre-push` (`transport.ts:137`).\n   Verified empirically 2026-07-27: git runs pre-push from the **common dir\n   only** — a hook under `.git/worktrees/<name>/hooks/` never executes. So a\n   repo whose first-ever cledger capture happens inside a worktree gets a dead\n   hook and the ledger silently never rides along on push. This repo was\n   unaffected only because `.git/hooks/pre-push` was already installed.\n2. `known-secrets.json` invisible → fails **open**: values taught to\n   capture-time redaction are not scrubbed during a worktree session, so a\n   known secret gets captured raw with nothing reporting it.\n3. `allowlist.json` invisible → fails closed: 213 findings from a worktree vs.\n   0 from the main checkout, same notes ref. Blocks the ledger push.\n4. `cursors/` reset → transcripts re-scanned from the top. Harmless (events\n   dedup by id), just wasted work. Same for `reanchor-cursor` and\n   `transport-warnings.json`.\n\n**Not affected:** the ledger data itself. Refs (incl.\n`refs/notes/conversation-ledger`), objects, and config (the fetch refspec) live\nin the common dir and are shared, so capture from a worktree writes to the\nright notes ref and sync works normally.\n\n**Likely fix:** `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` for the state directory and\nthe hook path. Cursors are the one piece that might arguably stay per-worktree,\nthough in practice each session id belongs to one cwd so sharing looks correct\ntoo — worth a moment's thought rather than a blind swap.\n\nNote this is invisible in normal use and only bites agents/humans working in\nworktrees, which is now common. See [[project-cledger-redaction-state]] for\nthe allowlist's role.\n","structuredPatch":[{"lines":[" ---"," name: project-cledger-worktree-gitdir","-description: \"cledger's per-repo local state is invisible from a git worktree — allowlist/cursors/known-secrets keyed on --absolute-git-dir\"","+description: cledger 0.13.0 — local state moved from per-worktree gitDir to the shared commonDir; also read-side dedup of duplicate event ids"," metadata: ","   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","-  modified: 2026-07-27T07:19:17.141Z","+  modified: 2026-07-27T07:36:05.431Z"," ---"," ","-Found 2026-07-27, unfixed. `findRepo` in `src/git.ts` sets `gitDir` from","-`git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir`, which in a worktree returns","-`.git/worktrees/<name>/`, not the shared `.git/`. All per-repo local state","-hangs off that path — `conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`,","-`known-secrets.json`, `cursors/`, `reanchor-cursor`, the pending queue.","+Found and fixed 2026-07-27, shipped in cledger 0.13.0 (on main, `47e117b`)."," ","-**Symptoms, worst first:**","-1. `installHook` writes to `repo.gitDir/hooks/pre-push` (`transport.ts:137`).","-   Verif