{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Both done.\n\n## Merge\n\n`main` is now `8edda18` and pushed. The feature branch is merged (`--no-ff`), then deleted locally and on origin; the worktree is removed; `git worktree list` shows only the main checkout, working tree clean. 143 tests pass on merged main. The cledger history went with it — `refs/notes/conversation-ledger` is at `624277a` locally and on origin, and `cledger sync` confirms nothing outstanding. I also rebuilt `dist/`, which the global `cledger` on your PATH symlinks into, so live captures now write the new fields.\n\nOn the PR: noted, and sorry for the extra step. My standing instructions for background jobs say to open a draft PR when I've made code changes in a worktree, so I did that by default rather than by reading it into your ask. GitHub detected the merge and auto-closed #1 as merged, so nothing is left open — but a PR record does now exist in the repo's history, and I can't undo that.\n\n## The worktree question\n\nYour understanding is right in substance. One correction: the git command isn't misbehaving. `git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir` does exactly what it documents. The wrong assumption was conceptual — that a repo has *one* git dir. Git deliberately gives each worktree its own at `.git/worktrees/<name>/` for per-worktree state (HEAD, index, reflogs), while shared state (refs, objects, config, hooks) stays in the common dir. So it resolves somewhere different from what we expected, but because we asked the wrong question, not because git surprised us.\n\nWhat's affected, worst first:\n\n1. **The pre-push hook — worse than what I reported earlier.** `installHook` writes to `repo.gitDir/hooks/pre-push`. I tested this directly just now: git runs pre-push from the **common dir only**, and a hook under `.git/worktrees/<name>/hooks/` never executes. So a repo whose first-ever cledger capture happens inside a worktree gets a hook git will never run, and the ledger silently never rides along on push. This repo escaped it only because `.git/hooks/pre-push` was already installed back in July.\n2. **`known-secrets.json` fails open.** Values you taught capture-time redaction to scrub aren't scrubbed during a worktree session, so a known secret gets captured raw — with nothing telling you.\n3. **`allowlist.json` fails closed.** The 213-vs-0 case from earlier. Noisy but visible, and the mildest of the three.\n4. **Cursors, reanchor-cursor, warning state** reset per worktree — transcripts re-scan from the top, but events dedup by id, so it's wasted work rather than corruption.\n\nWorth stating what is *not* broken, since it bounds the blast radius: the ledger data itself is fine. Refs, objects, and config all live in the common dir, which is why capture from the worktree wrote to the correct notes ref and why the merge and sync just now worked normally.\n\nThe fix is `--git-common-dir` for the state directory and the hook path. I'd not do it as a blind swap — cursors are the one piece where per-worktree could be defended, though in practice each session id belongs to a single cwd, so sharing them looks correct too. Want me to take it on?\n\nresult: Merged 0.12.0 into main (8edda18) and pushed with the cledger notes ref; branch and worktree removed, PR #1 auto-closed as merged — and confirmed the worktree bug is real and broader than first reported: cledger installs its pre-push hook where git will never run it, and known-secret redaction silently fails open inside a worktree.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"47e117b2e20969745be383f2ab62bcc21a3dc5a5","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295","seq":568},"id":"ev1-d7edeec5963f58f445fe502286855e0367283d7d199c01de29807d9851ce5767","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-27T07:19:34